     {
      "text": "74-year-old female presenting with excessive thirst and frequent urination for 5 weeks. Character: passing urine many times, also at night; radiation: n/a; aggravated by sweet food; relieved by nothing. Severity 6/10. Associated: blurred vision, tiredness, weight loss. PMH: Type 2 diabetes for 5 years; Appendectomy in 2017. Drugs: Metformin 500 mg. Allergy: sulfa drugs. Family: no similar illness. Personal: chews tobacco. Triage: ROUTINE."
